course: dictionary
lesson: 921
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so you need context to know which one is meant. Bleed most often means losing blood from the body, as in «For a small cut or graze, wash it with clean water, press with a clean cloth to stop bleeding». Pressing the cut helps stop the blood, so bleeding is blood leaving a wound.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. When a baby tooth comes out and «the gap bleeds», the clue is the gap in your mouth, so blood is coming from the gum. Ask: what word would fit here? Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Bleed can also describe colours that spread into each other, like dye bleeding in the wash. The sentence is the clue: colour is spreading onto other things, not blood leaving a body.
fact: Bleed is a verb: bleed, bleeds, bled, bleeding.
fact: «Bleeding» means losing blood from the body, because of a cut or injury.
fact: «Bleed» can also mean colours spreading into each other or onto other things.
fact: Heavy bleeding needs emergency help: press firmly with a clean cloth and tell an adult.
fact: Small cuts usually stop bleeding by themselves as blood clots and forms a scab.
exercise: In «press with a clean cloth to stop bleeding», what does bleeding mean? | Growing bigger each day | *Losing blood from a cut | Colours spreading into each other | Letting air out of a radiator
exercise: «When a baby tooth comes out and the gap bleeds, biting on clean gauze stops it.» What is bleeding? | The gauze | *The gap where the tooth was | The clean tissue | The tooth itself
exercise: Mum says the red top bled colour in the wash. What does bleed mean here? | Dried out | Shone brightly | *Spread into other things | Stopped moving
test: If someone is bleeding from a cut, what should you do? | Ignore it, because heavy bleeding always stops by itself | *Press firmly on it with a clean cloth and tell an adult | Wash the cut with dye | Laugh and wait until they feel better
test: What does the phrase «bleed to death» mean? | Turn a different colour | Fall fast asleep | *Lose so much blood that you die | Leak paint from a tin
exam: In ««No, not one little song,» replied the Rat firmly, though his heart bled», what does bled mean? | Let air out of a pipe | *Felt deep sadness inside | Lost blood from a cut | Spread colour onto paper
